# Hadith Archive — one canonical byte form on every platform.
# Supports docs/data-policy.md (UTF-8, NFC, LF line endings; byte-exact fingerprints).

# All text files: normalized to LF, never CRLF, on every operating system.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fonts: binary, kept byte for byte; the original TTF carries a digital signature.
*.ttf    binary
*.woff2  binary

# Core data: explicit text with LF, no re-encoding or content filters.
*.json   text eol=lf -filter -working-tree-encoding
*.jsonl  text eol=lf -filter -working-tree-encoding
